# inv-patch: 23-l3-rec
# purpose: L3 oracle, Mode D record density (spec I4 L3, H7): IAU_INV_REC_BYTES=16|32|64 sets the completion-callback record size on both sides (nvmf_tgt reads it once at transport create in iau_inv_rec_init(); the host library reads it at load time; same strtoll rule, any other value = the LOCKED 32 B). Layouts in 64-bit words, phase word written last: 32 B = LOCKED {cb_fn, cb_arg, cpl[0:8), cpl[8:16) with the ring phase at bit 48}, 2 per 64 B line; 16 B = {cb_arg, cpl[8:16)} with the ring phase at bit 48 (sqhd, sqid, cid, status: every field a Mode D completion uses), cb_fn kept once per qpair on the host (inv_cb_fn), 4 per line; 64 B = the 32 B record plus 32 B of padding never written or read, 1 per line. Target: iau_flush() keeps the original 32 B loop (instruction-identical at -O2 plus one load+compare+not-taken branch) and tail-calls an out-of-line 16/64 B flush; the record-ring map length is qsize x the size. Host (20's inv_flags architecture): the record ring is allocated at num_entries x the size; 16, exactly 32 and 64 set INV_F_REC16/INV_F_REC32/INV_F_REC64 on Mode D IO qpairs, so their completions run in inv_process_completions (inv_rec_pop and the record loops take a constant word count, dispatched once per poll). INV_F_REC32 is the L3 control: the LOCKED 32 B record through the same lever dispatch and loop shape as 16/64 B, so read rec16/rec64 against rec32 (the record-density effect) and rec32 against unset (the lever dispatch cost). The levers compose with 20 (trfree: with 16 B records the descriptor's w3 carries req, the record's w0 echoes it, cb_fn/cb_arg come from req) and 22 (I-thin: the thin read registers the qpair's cb_fn through a cold tail call); the tracker path (no 20/22) runs a copy of the stock lean Mode D loop that calls inv_cb_fn, registered at the first completion from the tr->cb_fn the unchanged stock submit stores (same line as tr->req) and checked against it per IO. With the env unset no bit is set, nvme_pcie_qpair_submit_request and nvme_pcie_qpair_process_completions compile to the same instructions as before (only __LINE__ immediates differ) and stock nvme_pcie_qpair offsets are unchanged (inv_cb_fn and inv_rec_logged at the tail)
# safety: SAFE for this workload (perf reads, one cb_fn per qpair, cdw0 unused); the record format != the LOCKED RTL/gem5 format (overlay only, never in spdk/)
# breaks: 16 B drops cpl dword0 (cdw0 + reserved; the host passes 0) and requires one cb_fn per qpair: a second cb_fn aborts the process (tracker path at its completion, before the callback runs; I-thin at its submit); record format != the LOCKED RTL format (overlay only); nvmf_tgt and the host must see the same IAU_INV_REC_BYTES (run_point exports it to both): a disagreement misparses every record and usually hangs perf (no timeout; it can also crash on a garbage callback), and check_l.py FAILs the point when the target's INV_REC line is missing, carries another env value, or gives other bytes than the host's construct lines; Mode D only (mode 0 ignores it); a host qpair with Mode E and a size other than 32 fails construct with -ENOTSUP; per-IO cycle records are not taken on the lever loops (non-lean builds only); oracle overhead the design would not pay: the per-IO tr->cb_fn check (16 B tracker path), one inv_flags test in 20's trfree submit and one in 22's thin read, one size dispatch per poll (lever loops, bounded by the rec32 control) and one load+compare per target flush. §4 L evidence (printed only when IAU_INV_REC_BYTES is non-empty, the target's rule): host "INV_REC qid=N bytes=B per_line=K inv_flags=0xNN" per Mode D IO qpair at construct and, at destroy, "INV_REC qid=N all K cids returned at destroy (bytes=B cb_fn=P)" only when that qpair's cid pool is whole (thin stack, else trfree stack, else every tracker on free_tr and outstanding_tr empty), else an ERROR line with "lost IO"; target "INV_REC target: env=V bytes=B per_line=K" at transport create; check_l.py expects one destroy line per qpair in mode 4 and the size agreement above
# env: IAU_INV_REC_BYTES=16|32|64, read by BOTH nvmf_tgt and the host (default 32; exactly 32 = the rec32 lever-loop control, unset = stock loops)
# base: 00-spin.diff,01-floor.diff,10-walk.diff,11-deadstores.diff,12-residue.diff,13-iport.diff,20-l1-trfree.diff,22-l2-thin.diff
